<title>USA: Delta Petroleum gets court ok to cut debt.</title>
<headline>Delta Petroleum gets court ok to cut debt.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Petroleum Corp said Thursday its agreement with Snyder Oil Corp and the Trustee in Bankruptcy for Underwriters Financial Group Inc, dated May 23, has been approved by the Bankruptcy Court.</p>
<p>The agreement will allow Delta to remove about $2,670,000 in current liability from its balance sheet thereby adding a like amount to Delta's shareholders' equity, the company explained.</p>
<p>This leaves the company with $1,077,180 of current liabilities and total liabilities, it added.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
